please welcome the filmmakers of dreams  awake kevin gordon and rebecca Meredith  wow this these last few days have been  absolutely surreal this is a tremendous  honor and we first and foremost want to  thank the Academy this has been a  wonderful experience and I think in  addition to being a tremendous honor  it's also been an amazing encouragement  to us as student filmmakers to continue  doing the work that we're doing so we  really really appreciate that we also  want to thank our program at Stanford  University the MFA documentary film and  video program there are some amazing  people there Dan pray with Jamie Meltzer  Johnny Simon's the technical staff  marker banach Christian gains Lee and  our other fourteen students who just  play a crucial role in the development  of our films and also our development as  filmmakers I want to thank my mother and  and Omar Romero and Jason Renault who  are here in support of me and also all  the friends and family who are back home  rooting for me and hoping that I don't  trip on the way up to the stage and I  just I can't thank all of these people  enough for helping me be here and  helping me believe in myself and and the  work that we're doing  um they asked us to do that we put the  finishing touches on this film just a  few days before the submission deadline  and really just sent it in as a why not  kind of attitude so this is just  absolutely amazing when my sister saw  the film she started to cry but she was  pregnant at the time so we didn't know  if it was the film or the hormones but I  guess it's the film for a large part I'd  really like to thank my family my sister  Lauren my brother-in-law Neal have been  incredible support and provide a lot of  feedback over the years my brother Byron  and my sister-in-law Lynn s who provided  support from afar and my parents  especially who are in the audience  tonight when I gave up on my lifelong  plans to be a lawyer and told them I was  going to pick up documentary filmmaking  they were naturally skeptical but  they've given me nothing then their  complete support so I thank them for  that as well as all my friends back home  and most importantly we want to thank  Doroteo Garcia the subject of our film  was just an incredibly inspiring  individual and it was an honor to be  able to share his poetry in his words  with other people and we'd also like to  thank the countless immigrants like him  who's amazing stories and contributions  to our society often go unnoticed thank  you
 

